\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 It\u8217 s been 30 years since the British author Philip Pullman published the first book in the beloved \u8220 His Dark Materials\u8221  trilogy, an epic adventure that also happens to be a daring retelling of Milton\u8217 s \u8220 Paradise Lost\u8221  in which the world is saved, rather than doomed, by original sin. Full of remarkable adventures alongside big ideas, the books introduced one of the most delightful devices in all of children\u8217 s literature: the animal daemons that reflect the characters\u8217  souls and are with them always.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 The trilogy concluded in 2000, but Pullman returned in 2017 with \u8220 La Belle Sauvage,\u8221  the first book in a new trilogy that continued the tale of his indomitable heroine, Lyra Silvertongue (and her daemon, a pine marten named Pantalaimon). An \u8220 equal rather than a sequel,\u8221  as Pullman calls it, the second trilogy jumps backward and then forward in time, as an older Lyra contends with a growing darkness in the world and within herself.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 And now Pullman, 79, is publishing \u8220 The Rose Field,\u8221  the final volume in the series he began so long ago. It\u8217 s hard to overstate how eagerly his readers have been waiting for this moment, and what it feels like to finally have in your hands a book you can\u8217 t wait to start but are reluctant to finish. Reading it means that this part of your life \u8212  the part with the book still in the future \u8212  is over.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb240\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 I first interviewed Pullman }{\field{\*\fldinst{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2  HYPERLINK }{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24
\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2  }{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 https://www.nytimes.com/2000/11/07/books/man-who-dared-make-religion-villain-british-author-s-trilogy-great-adventures.html}
{\*\datafield }}
{\fldrslt{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ul\cf1 in 2000}}}{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\loch\af2\dbch\af2
\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 , after I fell under the spell of his intoxicating, multi-world story and its dazzling characters: passionate witches; fearsome polar bears who wear finely wrought armor they forge themselves; a race of tiny, hotheaded spies who have deadly poison embedded in their spurs. Talking to him felt like reading his books. He operates on many levels at once, not unlike his alethiometer, a complex watch-like device full of symbols that allows its skilled users to find answers to difficult questions.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 I\u8217 m hardly the only one who has lost sleep over these books. A friend recently told me that, unable to stop reading the second book in the series, \u8220 The Subtle Knife,\u8221  while she was waiting to pick up her son at school more than 20 years go, she burst into sobs in public at the death of a beloved character. The best-selling British children\u8217 s author Katherine Rundell said in a recent interview that Lyra, \u8220 with her stubborn love and unruly vividness\u8221  is her \u8220 favorite heroine in English children\u8217 s literature.\u8221 }
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 \u8220 Pullman changed the field,\u8221  Rundell said. \u8220 He showed how much can be asked of a child reader, how eagerly they will rise to meet vast ideas. The books understand that children crave stories on the epic scale, that infinity is not too large for them.\u8221 }
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 And now here I am, meeting Pullman again after a quarter-century. We\u8217 re in the living room of the old farmhouse outside Oxford, England, that the author shares with Judith, his wife of 55 years and his first and best reader. (She appears briefly to say hello and to reveal that her own daemon is a tiny owl who \u8220 suddenly appeared one day.\u8221 ) The books and papers piled high on every available surface are testimony to the wild breadth of Pullman\u8217 s intellectual interests.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 Pullman is suffering from various physical ailments, including }{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b\i\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ul\cf2 long Covid}{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24
\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 , that have robbed him of some energy. But his conversation is as nimble and wide-ranging as ever. We\u8217 re interrupted from time to time by Mixie, the more boisterous of the household\u8217 s two cockapoos, who jumps on the sofa and offers me a stuffed alligator by way of greeting.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 Pullman decided to return to Lyra\u8217 s story, he said, because of where he\u8217 d left her back in 2000. Yes, she\u8217 d helped save the universe, but she was still so young, emerging from childhood into young adulthood. \u8220 What\u8217 s she going to do for the rest of her life?\u8221  he asked. \u8220 Learn Latin and French and play netball? I don\u8217 t think so.\u8221 }
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 \u8220 She needed another adventure,\u8221  he said. \u8220 Besides, she was getting to a stage in her life where interesting things go on.\u8221 }{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0
\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 In \u8220 La Belle Sauvage\u8221  (2017), which takes place before \u8220 His Dark Materials,\u8221  Lyra is an infant saved from her enemies and from a catastrophic flood by an industrious boy named Malcolm. Its sequel, \u8220 The Secret Commonwealth\u8221  (2019), jumps ahead to her life as a college student, at odds with both herself and the world around her, and \u8220 The Rose Field\u8221  begins the moment that story leaves off.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 The new book is full of wondrous things: Look especially for the touchy, egotistic gryphons, beasts with lions\u8217  bodies and eagles\u8217  heads, who worship gold and demand to be treated with elaborate respect. It\u8217 s also a plea for humanism and intellectual honesty in a world where the biggest villains are corporations, corrupt governments, a disdain for nature and a power-hungry, cruel church whose terrifying governing body is known as the Magisterium.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 Lyra and her daemon have separated after a painful falling-out, and in their different ways, both are on quests to recover her lost imagination \u8212  \u8220 the realm of the understanding\u8221  that includes \u8220 the mysteries of the heart and the mind.\u8221  Meanwhile, the Magisterium, propped up by its corrupt allies, is consolidating power and imposing its ideology on a cowed populace by way of disinformation, anti-science propaganda and violence.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 Pullman has always resisted overt discussion of how his books might comment on current events, but it\u8217 s not hard to see what themes are preoccupying him.}{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb240\sa0
\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 His writing works on two levels. On the surface is the story, which he sees as paramount. Underneath is an engagement with serious intellectual and metaphysical issues and a riot of allusions to other works \u8212  fairy tales, poems, novels, scientific treatises, philosophical texts, quantum physics \u8212  the fruits of a lifetime\u8217 s reading and study. If \u8220 Paradise Lost\u8221  was a driving force behind \u8220 His Dark Materials,\u8221  then Edmund Spenser\u8217 s 16th-century epic poem, }
{\field{\*\fldinst{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2  HYPERLINK }{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2  }{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 https://www.gutenberg.org/files/15272/15272-h/15272-h.htm}{\*\datafield }}
{\fldrslt{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ul\cf1 \u8220 The Faerie Queen,\u8221 }}}{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2  with its challenging episodic narrative, is an inspiration for the second trilogy.}{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260
\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 \u8220 I think a lot of the readers are surprised to find how steeped in history the books are and how much Pullman is borrowing from different historical elements and different literary texts,\u8221  said Kristen Poole, a professor of English at the University of Delaware and the author of \u8220 Philip Pullman and the Historical Imagination: Seventeenth-Century Literature, Science, and Religion in \u8216 His Dark Materials\u8217  and \u8216 The Book of Dust.\u8217 \u8221 }
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb240\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 A small sampling: Pullman borrowed the notion of the \u8220 secret commonwealth,\u8221  a shadowy world that includes spirits, fairies, ghosts and other uncanny beings, from a }{\field{\*\fldinst{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24
